      <article class="card card--top"><div class="card__body">
        <h3>Callao Bay &amp; San Lorenzo Island</h3>
        <p class="justify">A very calm voyage, recommended for groups looking to share a relaxed atmosphere without worrying about seasickness. It takes in La Punta and Cantolao beach, the yacht clubs, the Naval School, El Camotal, El Frontón Island with the ruins of the old prison, San Lorenzo Island with the Presidential Beach and Naval Base, the sunken ship, the port of Callao, Plaza Grau, the Real Felipe Fortress and Chucuito beach.</p>
      </div></article>
      <article class="card card--top-gold"><div class="card__body">
        <h3>Palomino Islands</h3>
        <p class="justify">Includes the whole route above and also reaches the Palomino Islands, home to the sea lions — where you can <strong>swim with them</strong>. You'll sail past San Lorenzo, El Frontón, Cavinzas and finally Palomino, also spotting guano birds and penguins.</p>
      </div></article>
